module

public import FormalConjecturesUtil

/-!
# Periods of the Bell numbers modulo $n$

The sequence gives the period $a(n)$ of the Bell numbers $B(m)$ modulo $n$: the least $k \ge 1$
such that $B(m + k) \equiv B(m) \pmod{n}$ for all $m \ge 0$.

*References:*
- [A054767](https://oeis.org/A054767), Eric W. Weisstein, 2002.
- [To33] J. Touchard, *Propriétés arithmétiques de certains nombres récurrents*, Ann. Soc. Sci.
  Bruxelles A 53 (1933), 21–31.
- [Ha34] M. Hall, *Arithmetic properties of a partition function*, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. 40
  (1934), 387.
- [Wi45] G. T. Williams, *Numbers generated by the function $e^{e^x - 1}$*, Amer. Math. Monthly
  52 (1945), 323–327.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace OeisA54767

/-- The Bell numbers modulo $p$. -/
def b (p n : ℕ) : ℕ := Nat.bell n % p

/-- The period of the Bell numbers modulo $n$: the least $k \ge 1$ such that
$B(m + k) \equiv B(m) \pmod{n}$ for all $m$. -/
noncomputable def a (n : ℕ) : ℕ := sInf {k | 0 < k ∧ ∀ m, b n (m + k) = b n m}

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_1 : a 1 = 1 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_2 : a 2 = 3 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_3 : a 3 = 13 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_4 : a 4 = 12 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_5 : a 5 = 781 := by
  sorry

/--
"For p prime, a(p) divides (p^p-1)/(p-1) = A023037(p), with equality at least for p up to 19."
- Unsigned comment in A054767.

The theorem states only the divisibility, in the equivalent form that $(p^p - 1)/(p - 1)$ is a
period of the Bell numbers modulo $p$. This is a classical theorem [To33, Ha34, Wi45]. Formal
proof by Wentao Li, with AI assistance. Its proof of Touchard's congruence is adapted from
[karlesmarin/formalizations](https://github.com/karlesmarin/formalizations/blob/1d089e08101adad7789f713473274d6d98fafc33/Formalizations/Combinatorics/Enumerative/Touchard.lean)
by Carles Marín, written with Claude as an AI assistant.
-/
@[category research solved, AMS 5 11, formal_proof using lean4 at
  "https://palomar-registry.org/entry.html?id=PALOMAR-2026-11-19-000003"]
theorem bell_period :
    ∀ p : ℕ, p.Prime → ∀ n : ℕ, b p (n + (p ^ p - 1) / (p - 1)) = b p n := by
  sorry

end OeisA54767
